  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1139 PM MST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nThe better potential for precipitation looks to shift toward\nsoutheastern NM on Saturday as the upper-level system continues\nsoutheastward. Overall, confidence remains low regarding the exact\ntrack, timing, and evolution of the disturbance, so precipitation\ncoverage and amounts could chance with future forecast updates. \n\nThe upper disturbance should gradually move away from NM over the\nweekend as broad ridging builds across the Great Basin and\nsouthern Rockies. This pattern will lead to generally dry\nconditions through the remainder of the period. Temperatures will\ngradually moderate, with the slightest warming trend into early \nnext week.",
